{"parse":{"title":"119th United States Congress","pageid":70645797,"text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"House_membership_changes\">House membership changes</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=119th_United_States_Congress&amp;veaction=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: House membership changes\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-divider\"> | </span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=119th_United_States_Congress&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section&#039;s source code: House membership changes\"><span>edit source</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1368532237\">.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}}</style><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_special_elections_to_the_United_States_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"List of special elections to the United States House of Representatives\">List of special elections to the United States House of Representatives</a></div>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n\n<caption>House changes\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr style=\"vertical-align:bottom;\">\n<th scope=\"col\">District\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Vacated by\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" data-sort-type=\"date\">Reason for change\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Successor\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" data-sort-type=\"date\"><span class=\"nowrap\">Date of successor's</span><br /><span class=\"nowrap\">formal installation<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SuccessorInstallation&#95;1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SuccessorInstallation-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>a<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></span>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Florida01&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Florida%27s_1st_congressional_district\" title=\"Florida&#39;s 1st congressional district\">Florida&#160;1</a></span>\n</th>\n<td>Vacant\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Matt_Gaetz\" title=\"Matt Gaetz\">Matt Gaetz</a> (R) resigned November 13, 2024, before the beginning of this Congress, and declined to take office after being re-elected.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />A <a href=\"/wiki/2025_Florida%27s_1st_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2025 Florida&#39;s 1st congressional district special election\">special election</a> was held on April 1, 2025.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Patronis, Jimmy\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Jimmy_Patronis\" title=\"Jimmy Patronis\">Jimmy Patronis</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>April 2, 2025\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Florida06&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Florida%27s_6th_congressional_district\" title=\"Florida&#39;s 6th congressional district\">Florida&#160;6</a></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Waltz, Mike\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mike_Waltz\" title=\"Mike Waltz\">Mike Waltz</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent resigned January 20, 2025, to become <a href=\"/wiki/National_Security_Advisor_(United_States)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"National Security Advisor (United States)\">National Security Advisor</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Trumps&#95;Taps&#95;Rep.&#95;Mike&#95;Waltz&#95;as&#95;National&#95;Security&#95;Advisor&#95;3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Trumps_Taps_Rep._Mike_Waltz_as_National_Security_Advisor-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Waltz&#95;4-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Waltz-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />A <a href=\"/wiki/2025_Florida%27s_6th_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2025 Florida&#39;s 6th congressional district special election\">special election</a> was held on April 1, 2025.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Fine, Randy\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Randy_Fine\" title=\"Randy Fine\">Randy Fine</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>April 2, 2025\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Texas18&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Texas%27s_18th_congressional_district\" title=\"Texas&#39;s 18th congressional district\">Texas&#160;18</a></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span class=\"nowrap\"><span data-sort-value=\"Turner, Sylvester\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Sylvester_Turner\" title=\"Sylvester Turner\">Sylvester Turner</a></span></span></span></span><br />(D)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent died March 5, 2025.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Turner&#95;5-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Turner-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-6\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />A <a href=\"/wiki/2025%E2%80%9326_Texas%27s_18th_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2025–26 Texas&#39;s 18th congressional district special election\">special election</a> was held on November 4, 2025, and a runoff was held on January 31, 2026.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"Menefee, Christian\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Christian_Menefee\" title=\"Christian Menefee\">Christian Menefee</a></span></span></span><br />(D)\n</td>\n<td>February 2, 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Arizona07&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Arizona%27s_7th_congressional_district\" title=\"Arizona&#39;s 7th congressional district\">Arizona&#160;7</a></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"Grijalva, Raúl\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ra%C3%BAl_Grijalva\" title=\"Raúl Grijalva\">Raúl Grijalva</a></span></span></span><br />(D)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent died March 13, 2025, having already planned to retire at the end of the term.<br />A <a href=\"/wiki/2025_Arizona%27s_7th_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2025 Arizona&#39;s 7th congressional district special election\">special election</a> was held on September 23, 2025.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"Grijalva, Adelita\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Adelita_Grijalva\" title=\"Adelita Grijalva\">Adelita Grijalva</a></span></span></span><br />(D)\n</td>\n<td>November 12, 2025\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Virginia11&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Virginia%27s_11th_congressional_district\" title=\"Virginia&#39;s 11th congressional district\">Virginia&#160;11</a></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"Connolly, Gerry\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Gerry_Connolly\" title=\"Gerry Connolly\">Gerry Connolly</a></span></span></span><br />(D)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent died May 21, 2025, having already planned to retire at the end of the term.<br />A <a href=\"/wiki/2025_Virginia%27s_11th_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2025 Virginia&#39;s 11th congressional district special election\">special election</a> was held on September 9, 2025.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span class=\"nowrap\"><span data-sort-value=\"Walkinshaw, James\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/James_Walkinshaw\" title=\"James Walkinshaw\">James Walkinshaw</a></span></span></span></span><br />(D)\n</td>\n<td>September 10, 2025\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Tennessee07&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Tennessee%27s_7th_congressional_district\" title=\"Tennessee&#39;s 7th congressional district\">Tennessee&#160;7</a></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Green, Mark\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mark_Green_(Tennessee_politician)\" title=\"Mark Green (Tennessee politician)\">Mark Green</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent resigned July 20, 2025, to take a job in the private sector.<br />A <a href=\"/wiki/2025_Tennessee%27s_7th_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2025 Tennessee&#39;s 7th congressional district special election\">special election</a> was held on December 2, 2025.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Van Epps, Matt\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Matt_Van_Epps\" title=\"Matt Van Epps\">Matt Van Epps</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>December 4, 2025\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span class=\"nowrap\"><span data-sort-value=\"New Jersey11&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/New_Jersey%27s_11th_congressional_district\" title=\"New Jersey&#39;s 11th congressional district\">New Jersey&#160;11</a></span></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"Sherrill, Mikie\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mikie_Sherrill\" title=\"Mikie Sherrill\">Mikie Sherrill</a></span></span></span><br />(D)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent resigned November 20, 2025, after being <a href=\"/wiki/2025_New_Jersey_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2025 New Jersey gubernatorial election\">elected</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Governor_of_New_Jersey\" title=\"Governor of New Jersey\">Governor of New Jersey</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-7\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />A <a href=\"/wiki/2026_New_Jersey%27s_11th_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2026 New Jersey&#39;s 11th congressional district special election\">special election</a> was held on April 16, 2026.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"Mejia, Analilia\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Analilia_Mejia\" title=\"Analilia Mejia\">Analilia Mejia</a></span></span></span><br />(D)\n</td>\n<td>April 20, 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span class=\"nowrap\"><span data-sort-value=\"Georgia14&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Georgia%27s_14th_congressional_district\" title=\"Georgia&#39;s 14th congressional district\">Georgia&#160;14</a></span></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Greene, Marjorie Taylor\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Marjorie_Taylor_Greene\" title=\"Marjorie Taylor Greene\">Marjorie Taylor Greene</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent resigned January 5, 2026, citing her disagreements with President <a href=\"/wiki/Donald_Trump\" title=\"Donald Trump\">Donald Trump</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-8\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />A <a href=\"/wiki/2026_Georgia%27s_14th_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2026 Georgia&#39;s 14th congressional district special election\">special election</a> was held on March 10, 2026, and a runoff was held on April 7.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Fuller, Clay\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Clay_Fuller\" title=\"Clay Fuller\">Clay Fuller</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>April 14, 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span class=\"nowrap\"><span data-sort-value=\"California01&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/California%27s_1st_congressional_district\" title=\"California&#39;s 1st congressional district\">California&#160;1</a></span></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"LaMalfa, Doug\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Doug_LaMalfa\" title=\"Doug LaMalfa\">Doug LaMalfa</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent died January 6, 2026.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-9\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />A <a href=\"/wiki/2026_California%27s_1st_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2026 California&#39;s 1st congressional district special election\">special election</a> was held on June 2, 2026.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span class=\"nowrap\"><span data-sort-value=\"Gallagher, James\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/James_Gallagher_(California_politician)\" title=\"James Gallagher (California politician)\">James Gallagher</a></span></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>June 10, 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span class=\"nowrap\"><span data-sort-value=\"California03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/California%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"California&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">California&#160;3</a></span></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Kiley, Kevin\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Kevin_Kiley_(politician)\" title=\"Kevin Kiley (politician)\">Kevin Kiley</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent changed parties March 9, 2026.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-10\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</td>\n<td style=\"background:#fc5b5b\"><span class=\"nowrap\"><span data-sort-value=\"Kiley, Kevin\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Kevin_Kiley_(politician)\" title=\"Kevin Kiley (politician)\">Kevin Kiley</a></span></span></span></span><br />(I)\n</td>\n<td>March 9, 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span class=\"nowrap\"><span data-sort-value=\"California14&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/California%27s_14th_congressional_district\" title=\"California&#39;s 14th congressional district\">California&#160;14</a></span></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"Swalwell, Eric\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eric_Swalwell\" title=\"Eric Swalwell\">Eric Swalwell</a></span></span></span><br />(D)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent resigned April 14, 2026, following sexual assault allegations.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-11\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />A <a href=\"/wiki/2026_California%27s_14th_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2026 California&#39;s 14th congressional district special election\">special election</a> was held on June 16, 2026, and a runoff was held on August 18.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"Wahab, Aisha\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Aisha_Wahab\" title=\"Aisha Wahab\">Aisha Wahab</a></span></span></span><br />(D)\n</td>\n<td>September 2, 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span class=\"nowrap\"><span data-sort-value=\"Texas23&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Texas%27s_23rd_congressional_district\" title=\"Texas&#39;s 23rd congressional district\">Texas&#160;23</a></span></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Gonzales, Tony\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Tony_Gonzales\" title=\"Tony Gonzales\">Tony Gonzales</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent resigned April 14, 2026, after admitting to an affair.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-12\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-12\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" colspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">Vacant until the next Congress\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span class=\"nowrap\"><span data-sort-value=\"Florida20&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Florida%27s_20th_congressional_district\" title=\"Florida&#39;s 20th congressional district\">Florida&#160;20</a></span></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"Cherfilus-McCormick, Sheila\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Sheila_Cherfilus-McCormick\" title=\"Sheila Cherfilus-McCormick\">Sheila Cherfilus-McCormick</a></span></span></span><br />(D)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent resigned April 21, 2026, following money laundering allegations.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-13\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-13\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>12<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Georgia13&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Georgia%27s_13th_congressional_district\" title=\"Georgia&#39;s 13th congressional district\">Georgia&#160;13</a></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"Scott, David\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/David_Scott_(Georgia_politician)\" title=\"David Scott (Georgia politician)\">David Scott</a></span></span></span><br />(D)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent died April 22, 2026.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-14\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-14\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>13<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />A <a href=\"/wiki/2026_Georgia%27s_13th_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2026 Georgia&#39;s 13th congressional district special election\">special election</a> was held on July 28, 2026, and a runoff was held on August 25.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"Blair, Everton\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Everton_Blair\" title=\"Everton Blair\">Everton Blair</a></span></span></span><br />(D)\n</td>\n<td>September 1, 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span class=\"nowrap\"><span data-sort-value=\"Oklahoma01&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Oklahoma%27s_1st_congressional_district\" title=\"Oklahoma&#39;s 1st congressional district\">Oklahoma&#160;1</a></span></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Hern, Kevin\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Kevin_Hern\" title=\"Kevin Hern\">Kevin Hern</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent resigning on November 30, 2026, to succeed appointed senator <a href=\"/wiki/Alan_Armstrong\" title=\"Alan Armstrong\">Alan Armstrong</a> after winning the <a href=\"/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_election_in_Oklahoma\" title=\"2026 United States Senate election in Oklahoma\">2026 election</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Hern&#95;15-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Hern-15\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" colspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">Vacant until the next Congress\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span class=\"nowrap\"><span data-sort-value=\"California34&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/California%27s_34th_congressional_district\" title=\"California&#39;s 34th congressional district\">California&#160;34</a></span></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"Gomez, Jimmy\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Jimmy_Gomez\" title=\"Jimmy Gomez\">Jimmy Gomez</a></span></span></span><br />(D)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent resigning on December 1, 2026, following sexual assault allegations.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-16\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-16\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>15<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br /><span class=\"error mw-ext-cite-error\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">Cite error: There are <code>&lt;ref&#160;group&#61;lower-alpha&gt;</code> tags&#160;or <code>&#123;&#123;efn&#125;&#125;</code> templates on this page, but the references will not show without a <code>&#123;&#123;reflist&#124;group&#61;lower-alpha&#125;&#125;</code> template&#160;or <code>&#123;&#123;notelist&#125;&#125;</code> template (see the <a href=\"/wiki/Help:Cite_errors/Cite_error_group_refs_without_references\" title=\"Help:Cite errors/Cite error group refs without references\">help page</a>).</span></p><div class=\"mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1333433106\">.mw-parser-output cite.citation{font-style:inherit;word-wrap:break-word}.mw-parser-output .citation q{quotes:\"\\\"\"\"\\\"\"\"'\"\"'\"}.mw-parser-output .citation:target{background-color:rgba(0,127,255,0.133)}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-free.id-lock-free a{background:url(\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/65/Lock-green.svg\")right 0.1em center/9px no-repeat}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-limited.id-lock-limited a,.mw-parser-output .id-lock-registration.id-lock-registration a{background:url(\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/Lock-gray-alt-2.svg\")right 0.1em center/9px no-repeat}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-subscription.id-lock-subscription a{back